{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And you shall know</b> — from the exodus from Egypt, that YHWH your Elohim, He is the Elohim, who created heaven and earth, as I explained (Ramban on Deuteronomy 6:20). And further, you shall know from this that He is the faithful El, whose word does not return void, and that He keeps the covenant and the kindness to those who love Him and to those who keep His commandments, those who fear His name, for a thousand generations, in their seed, just as He kept the covenant of your fathers for you. And you shall know that He repays those who hate Him their wickedness to the face of each one of them, to destroy them, just as He destroyed the Egyptians and did not delay for them. And this attribute that He mentioned — truth forever: even though there is a wicked person who prolongs in his wickedness, this will not be so for him except because of this attribute mentioned, that He keeps kindness — and behold, he has done some good for which He must repay him. If so, there are in the attributes of the Holy One, blessed be He, only these two attributes: repaying good for good and repaying evil for evil. And it is possible that His confirmed haters are those who deny His divinity, and they have no merit whatsoever; as they said (Ecclesiastes Rabbah 7:32): Rabbi Yoshiah said, for three things the Holy One, blessed be He, extends His patience to the wicked in this world: perhaps they will repent, or they have performed commandments whose reward the Holy One, blessed be He, will pay in this world, or perhaps righteous ones will emerge from them — for thus we find that He extended His patience to Ahaz and Hezekiah emerged from him, and also to Amon and Josiah emerged from him, and also to Shimei and Mordecai emerged from him. And none of these are included among His haters. And there is a sod in the phrase <b>to his face</b> concerning the wicked one who has it good. And He returned: 'and you shall keep the commandment,' etc. — to say: therefore you shall keep the commandment and the statutes and the ordinances, so that you will not be among His haters who perish, but rather among those who love Him and keep His commandments, who are remembered for good and for life."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The phrase וְהֶחְזִיר is obscure; rendered hyper-literally as 'And He returned,' possibly a textual corruption."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:46:36.456151149Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}